                <pb facs="0701" n="581" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg581"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.248/34: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-19T16:00:00-06:00">June 19, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>130. Department’s telegram of June 12, 2 p.m. … sold his plane to the Honduran
                    Government yesterday and states he is leaving Honduras in a few days. His plane
                    is now being piloted by Honduran aviator …, of limited flying ability, and is
                    carrying small bombs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
